/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (In today's digital age, screen time dependency has become a significant and pressing concern across different age groups and regions. The ubiquity of smartphones, tablets, and digital platforms has fundamentally reshaped how we interact, communicate, and consume information. Studies highlight the rising hours spent on screens have the potential to impair focus and lead to feelings of isolation, anxiety, and even depression. Moreover, productivity and self-control are also at stake, as endless scrolling and constant notifications diminish the ability to concentrate on tasks and personal goals.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (As screen time continues to rise globally, it is crucial to assess its broader implications on mental health and societal well-being. Recognizing these impacts can empower individuals to adopt healthier digital habits and foster a more balanced relationship with technology.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
